{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":29,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:riemannian-metric","uses":[],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:riemannian-metric","line":79,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Riemannian Metric]\n\\label{def:riemannian-metric}\n\n\n\n\nA Riemannian metric on a smooth manifold $M$ is a smooth covariant $2$-tensor $g$ whose value $g_p$ is an inner product on $T_pM$ for every $p$. A Riemannian manifold is a pair $(M,g)$.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Riemannian Metric] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7269656d616e6e69616e2d6d6574726963\"></span> <p></p>A Riemannian metric on a smooth manifold <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is a smooth covariant <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$2$\">$2$</span>-tensor <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g$\">$g$</span> whose value <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g_p$\">$g_p$</span> is an inner product on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_pM$\">$T_pM$</span> for every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span>. A Riemannian manifold is a pair <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span>. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:inner-product-spaces-linearly-isometric","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:convex-inner-products","relations":[],"backlinks":[{"kind":